          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Foundations of Artificial Intelligence"
            }
          ],
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.389,
            0.603,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Bart Selman",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.327,
            0.497,
            0.69,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reinforcement Learning R&N – Chapter 21",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.707,
            0.844,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note: in the next two parts of RL, some of the figure/section numbers refer to an earlier edition of R&N with a more basic description of the techniques.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.884,
            0.721,
            0.933
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The slides provide a self-contained description.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.057,
            0.962,
            0.123
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reinforcement Learning"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.06,
            0.155,
            0.843,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In our discussion of Search methods (developed for problem solving), we assumed a given State Space and operators that lead from one State to one or more Successor states with a possible operator Cost.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.06,
            0.464,
            0.958,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The State space can be exponentially large but is in principle known. The difficulty was finding the right path (sequence of moves). This problem solved by searching through the various alternative sequences of moves. In tough spaces, this leads to exponential searches.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.061,
            0.849,
            0.877,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can we do something totally different?? Avoid search…",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.077,
            0.079,
            0.906,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why don’t we “just learn” how to make the right move in each possible state?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.077,
            0.303,
            0.905,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In principle, need to know very little about environment at the start. Simply observe another agent / human / program make steps (go from state to state) and mimic!",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.076,
            0.677,
            0.945,
            0.967
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reinforcement learning: Some of the earliest AI research (1960s). It works! Principles and ideas still applicable today… Led to AlphaGo by Google. (World’s best Go player, 2016.)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.079,
            0.531,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ":AlphaGo"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.05,
            0.077,
            0.531,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
